-- Arena challenges batch 11/14: rows 251-275 (track: Control Systems, category: EEE)

e_ss = 1 / (1 + K_p) where K_p = K','{"choices": ["0", "1/10", "1/11", "1"], "correct": 2}'::jsonb,'Position error constant K_p = lim(s→0) G(s) = K = 10. Steady-state error e_ss = 1/(1+K_p) = 1/(1+10) = 1/11 ≈ 0.091 or 9.1%. For zero steady-state error to a step: need at least one integrator (Type 1 system).','{multiple_choice}'::text[],0.8) ON CONFLICT (slug) DO NOTHING;

Ω(s)/V_a(s) = K_m / (τ_m × s + 1)

What does the motor time constant τ_m represent?','{"choices": ["The time to reach maximum speed", "The electrical L/R time constant of the armature", "The mechanical time constant — time for motor speed to reach 63.2% of final speed after a voltage step; determined by J (inertia) and B (damping)", "The commutator switching period"], "correct": 2}'::jsonb,'τ_m = J/B (mechanical: inertia/friction). τ_e = L/R (electrical: inductance/resistance). For control design, τ_m >> τ_e typically, so τ_e is often neglected. τ_m determines how fast the motor responds to command changes.','{multiple_choice}'::text[],0.76) ON CONFLICT (slug) DO NOTHING;

Calculate K_P, T_I, T_D.','{"choices": ["K_P=100, T_I=1, T_D=0.125", "K_P=120, T_I=0.25, T_D=0.0625", "K_P=120, T_I=2, T_D=1", "K_P=200, T_I=0.5, T_D=0.0625"], "correct": 1}'::jsonb,'K_P = 0.6 × 200 = 120. T_I = 0.5/2 = 0.25 s. T_D = 0.5/8 = 0.0625 s. Z-N tuning is aggressive (often 25% overshoot) — usually detune by factor 1.5–2 for better robustness.','{multiple_choice}'::text[],0.65) ON CONFLICT (slug) DO NOTHING;

s² + 2ζωₙs + ωₙ² = 0','{"choices": ["ζ=0.5, ωₙ=4 rad/s", "ζ=0.5, ωₙ=2 rad/s", "ζ=1, ωₙ=2 rad/s", "ζ=0.25, ωₙ=2 rad/s"], "correct": 1}'::jsonb,'ωₙ² = 4 → ωₙ = 2 rad/s. 2ζωₙ = 2 → ζ = 2/(2×2) = 0.5. Since 0 < ζ < 1: underdamped system with oscillatory step response. Settling time ≈ 4/(ζωₙ) = 4/1 = 4 s.','{multiple_choice}'::text[],0.7) ON CONFLICT (slug) DO NOTHING;
